      "writtenOn": "2021-03-03T20:03:15Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Instead of making an exception here (hard to maintain and read), could you apply this logic in the caller?\n\nFrom code analysis, it seems that the only impacted caller is writeIncomingSmsSessionWithType().\n\nIn terms of defining the logic inside writeIncomingSmsSessionWithType(), I think we could calculate\n - offset \u003d timestamps[0] - SystemClock.elapsedRealtime();\n - for each event, use timestamp \u003d timestamps[i] - offset\n\nIn this way, we correctly capture the delays between events, without mixing different sources of time (as some SMS events are anyway calculated using SystemClock.elapsedRealtime()).",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 109,
        "startChar": 8,
        "endLine": 119,
        "endChar": 9
      },
      "revId": "e1a0f0c806ee0ee4af6a93b35e0dac203aed5503",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "0d3ed15f_628e4541",
        "filename": "src/java/com/android/internal/telephony/metrics/InProgressSmsSession.java",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 119,
      "author": {
        "id": 1121603
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-03-04T02:27:46Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "By this CL, the delay will be the time interval between the current time and SCTS. However,\n\nwriteIncomingSmsSessionWithType(..., timestamps[], ...) {\n    offset \u003d timestamps[0] - SystemClock.elapsedRealtime();\n    FOR(i) {\n        smsSession.addEvent(timestamps[i] - offset, ...);\n    }\n}\nNamely,\nIf A \u003d SystemClock.elapsedRealtime();\n1st part or single SMS \u003d\u003e smsSession.addEvent(A, ...); \u003d\u003e Maybe, the delay will be 1 always.\n\n2nd part \u003d\u003e smsSession.addEvent(A + interval between 1st and 2nd part , ...);\n..\ni-th part \u003d\u003e smsSession.addEvent(A + interval between 1st and i-th part , ...);\n\nAre they expected result?",
      "parentUuid": "68b9f997_c6d1d600",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 109,
        "startChar": 8,
        "endLine": 119,
        "endChar": 9
      },
      "revId": "e1a0f0c806ee0ee4af6a93b35e0dac203aed5503",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "5ab16191_791c0f00",
        "filename": "src/java/com/android/internal/telephony/metrics/InProgressSmsSession.java",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 119,
      "author": {
        "id": 1407086
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-03-09T00:23:43Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The SmsSession is a sequence of events and the delay tracks the (rounded) time between one event and the next one. If we apply a different formula only for some events, we would end up with values that might not be valid and consistent.\n\nEven assuming that SCTS and SystemClock.elapsedRealtime() are aligned (which I doubt is true in general), this formula would lead to much larger delay values (SCTS is much older), as they account for delays that are outside the control of the device.\n\nThe goal is to track the relative delay of events between each other.",
      "parentUuid": "0d3ed15f_628e4541",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 109,
        "startChar": 8,
        "endLine": 119,
        "endChar": 9
      },
